  "$comment": "Go HTTP clients read from tables (`ClientSpec` in src/lang/ir/language.ts); `imports` are Go import paths. `net/http`: the package functions (`http.Get(url)`, `http.Post(url, contentType, body)`, `http.PostForm(url, values)`) and the same methods of a `http.Client` (`&http.Client{}`, `http.DefaultClient`, a field or parameter of type `*http.Client`); requests built with `http.NewRequest` are read by `nethttp.ts`. The fhttp fork and go-retryablehttp keep the same API. Resty v2 and v3: `resty.New()` with its client settings, then `R()` and the request's (`SetHeader`, `SetBody`, `SetQueryParam`), sent by a verb method.",
